  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the line $a x+b y+c=0, a b \\neq 0,$ is a tangent\r\nto the curve $x y=1-2 x,$ then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ogBx2",
      "text": "$a>0, b    < 0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "s2XI1",
      "text": "$a>0, b>0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "plDll",
      "text": "$a    < 0, b>0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "QNCeG",
      "text": "$a    < 0, b < 0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $xy=1-2 x$\r\n$\\Rightarrow y=\\frac{1-2 x}{x}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{-2 x-(1-2 x) \\cdot 1}{x^{2}}$\r\n$\\quad=\\frac{-2 x-1+2 x}{x^{2}}=\\frac{-1}{x^{2}}    < 0$\r\nsince, $a x+b y+c=0$ is tangent to the curve $xy=1-2 x$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{-a}{b} < 0 \\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{b}>0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow$ Either $a>b>0$ or $a < 0, b < 0$",
    "image": null
  },
